process-places.m's processes on the machine's GPU (docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU
processes that run loops, one kernel for a GPU's processes): processes of
one module that run one after another, a spawn of another module's kind
while the first module's kernel runs, phases that follow each other once a
monitor says the last one's process ended, a host process that receives
from a GPU process's mailbox, and spawns until the kernel has no free wave,
which fail rather than wait. The program then ends while the
kernel's waves wait for messages.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch -I %S/Inputs %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/place_phase.m %S/process-places.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 | FileCheck %S/process-places.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: not %gpu-env %t2 other 2>&1 | FileCheck %S/process-places.m --check-prefix=OTHER
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 phases | FileCheck %S/process-places.m --check-prefix=PHASES --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: not %gpu-env %t2 steal 2>&1 | FileCheck %S/process-places.m --check-prefix=STEAL
RUN: not %gpu-env %t2 full 2>&1 | FileCheck %S/process-places.m --check-prefix=FULL

The waves that a process has run are free again, and what it had is freed.
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 %t2 phases 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FREED --match-full-lines
FREED:11 normal 22 noproc
FREED:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
FREED:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
